From 9030969b809a417e3c67ce9bc0ff228c7475e35b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:54:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(ggml-cpu): read each Q8_0 expert row once for up to 4
 tokens, and prefetch it

An MTP verify step gives each routed expert 1 to 4 rows. mul_mat_id's
one_chunk path called vec_dot once per (expert row, token), so a row was
read once per token. ggml_vec_dot_q8_0_q8_0_ncols computes a block of up
to 16 expert rows against up to 4 tokens: each x block is loaded once for
all columns, and each column keeps vec_dot's own accumulator, block order
and horizontal sum, so the output is bit for bit the same. It prefetches
4 KiB ahead, about one line per block, past the hardware prefetcher's stop
at each page. Other architectures run the vec_dot loop as before.

On koishi (Xeon Gold 6150, node 0 quiet, 18 threads), three alternating
rounds: the 4-token expert matmul at the model's shapes 597-604 to
543-557 us (gate) and 612-622 to 547-559 us (down); a 4-token verify step
311.9 / 311.2 / 309.6 to 303.8 / 305.2 / 307.5 ms. Prompt reads are
unchanged: experts with 4 or more rows take the sgemm path. An AVX-512BW
integer part was slower on this CPU and is not in.

Perplexity identical to the last digit; an exactness test of 27000
outputs found no difference.
